# Where the project is, and the key to read it with.
#
# The base URL is everything before `/v1`, and which it is depends on how the project is
# being served:
#
#   nineveh run --serve   one project, at the root    http://127.0.0.1:4000
#   nineveh up            many, each under its name   http://127.0.0.1:4000/projects/market
#   hosted                                            https://api.nineveh.dev/projects/market
#
# The default is the first, and loopback in local mode needs no key, so leave both unset
# for that. Against a hosted project, paste its URL and a read key from Studio →
# Settings → API keys. The key reaches the browser, which is fine: reads never touch the
# chain, so an exposed read key spends no stream credit.
VITE_NINEVEH_PROJECT=http://127.0.0.1:4000
VITE_NINEVEH_KEY=
